                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c40c45ba-f269-4613-b2b3-234b177bbc25",
                        "entry_id": "5c5821ee-8b84-326c-98ed-74d00a2cf30d",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "louchest"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "683271e6-61ab-3240-8173-4deebd548e0f",
                        "entry_id": "5c5821ee-8b84-326c-98ed-74d00a2cf30d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of questionable taste or morality; decadent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aaaae0d2-8ed2-462b-b9c9-7676f0b482bb",
                                "sense_id": "683271e6-61ab-3240-8173-4deebd548e0f",
                                "text": "Upstairs Downstairs hosts the Kennedys and Wallis Simpson (these days, in British culture, the archetypal louche American)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75f2083a-a862-48b6-a4f2-2b2ba04a79ab",
                                "sense_id": "683271e6-61ab-3240-8173-4deebd548e0f",
                                "text": "Ever since X-Men: First Class set the series' clock back a few decades and installed Michael Fassbender's moody Magneto and James McAvoy's louche Charles Xavier as replacements for Ian McKellen and Patrick Stewart's chess-playing pappies, the big-screen X-Men's central conflict—Xavier's Booker T. Washington-esque School For Gifted Youngsters vs. a rogue's gallery of evil mutants, crew cuts, and politicos—has gotten a lot murkier."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf2fa3be-1dfb-37b6-befd-df21e78cb0fc",
                        "entry_id": "5c5821ee-8b84-326c-98ed-74d00a2cf30d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not reputable or decent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a84d5a7f-70e7-4230-928e-bd2fe3940555",
                                "sense_id": "cf2fa3be-1dfb-37b6-befd-df21e78cb0fc",
                                "text": "My uncle knows something about that fellow—Clavering knows something about him. There’s something louche regarding him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b01e99d7-cd47-4e4f-8490-275b30e1f0ff",
                                "sense_id": "cf2fa3be-1dfb-37b6-befd-df21e78cb0fc",
                                "text": "The aunt will refuse; she will think the whole proceeding very louche!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6eadff9c-f3e5-3c34-98ed-286cba5f9876",
                        "entry_id": "5c5821ee-8b84-326c-98ed-74d00a2cf30d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unconventional and slightly disreputable in an attractive manner; raffish, rakish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40b51945-e160-4b23-af17-3934d1dfbc68",
                                "sense_id": "6eadff9c-f3e5-3c34-98ed-286cba5f9876",
                                "text": "Anyone inside the business can also tell you that without Carine Roitfeld's louche sexy styling Tom Ford's Gucci might easily have come off looking like a high-end Club Monaco."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b5171e6a-c462-3d8a-b2bb-718fdcaf3fda",
                "word": "louche",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22e6d76e-5547-318f-96f9-ca9c839287fc",
                        "entry_id": "b5171e6a-c462-3d8a-b2bb-718fdcaf3fda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dubious or disreputable person or thing"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a93f05fd-eca5-48a5-9c42-bbda2bbc9827",
                                "sense_id": "22e6d76e-5547-318f-96f9-ca9c839287fc",
                                "text": "'That's right,' Joe smiled. 'Loafing about on the Mall with the louche of the town. And, speaking of the louche of the town, don't we have an appointment to interview one or two of them this morning?'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1149cb2c-7280-4ec0-b61d-fa9ae113bcbf",
                                "sense_id": "22e6d76e-5547-318f-96f9-ca9c839287fc",
                                "text": "I'm outraged this louche has since fathered two children with another woman and that after all this questionable, nefarious behavior, Greer continues to see no conflict of interest in him being Terd's guardian."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2e576d0-1203-4ae4-a4d6-8b64a673edf2",
                                "sense_id": "22e6d76e-5547-318f-96f9-ca9c839287fc",
                                "text": "\"Rooster, you say? He seems to always appear at unusual times and locations. He strikes me as something of a legerdemain. Let's hope he is no louche when it comes to his role in all of this."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "eab7071f-de3a-3dda-b927-518204012626",
